load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# First-order logic: the logic of quantifiers over individuals, with predicates, functions, and the connectives, able to
# say "for all x" and "there exists x" about elements but not about sets of them. It is the standard language of
# mathematics, complete (every valid sentence is provable) and compact (a theory has a model if every finite part does).
# The form carries the set of symbols (the signature); the quantifiers, connectives, and inference rules are the logic.
form first-order-logic
  link symbols, like set
